## Startup & bootstrap flow

### Entry point

- `src/Bible.Alarm/MauiProgram.cs`
  - registers libraries (CommunityToolkit MediaElement, Syncfusion)
  - calls `ServiceRegistrationHelper.RegisterServices(builder.Services)`

### Bootstrap orchestration

- `src/Bible.Alarm/Services/Bootstrap/BootstrapOrchestrator.cs`
  - runs core init in parallel:
    - DB init/migrations (`IDatabaseBootstrapService`)
    - Fluxor init (`IFluxorBootstrapService`)
    - resource copy (`IResourceBootstrapService`, e.g. embedded files)
  - sends an `InitializedMessage` early to show UI while schedules load
  - loads schedules into Fluxor state (`IScheduleBootstrapService`)
  - runs platform bootstrap (`IPlatformBootstrapService`) for channels/jobs

### Why “bootstrap can run from multiple entrypoints”

Android Auto, alarm receivers, etc. can start the process without the UI. The bootstrap is guarded so it runs once, and the UI can re-trigger schedule loading if needed.

