## Technology choices (what to remember when editing)

- **DI (`Microsoft.Extensions.DependencyInjection`)**:
  - **Why**: keeps MAUI UI code thin; enables platform-specific swapping behind shared interfaces (`INotificationService`, storage, etc.)
  - **How**: most services are registered as singletons; DbContexts are scoped
  - **Where**: `src/Bible.Alarm/Common/Helpers/ServiceRegistrationHelper.cs`
- **Fluxor**:
  - **Why**: centralizes schedule/editor state + avoids “who owns truth?” across many modals/pages + Android Auto/CarPlay
  - **Rule**: reducers are pure; async/IO belongs in effects
  - **Where**: `src/Bible.Alarm/Stores/**` (notably `Stores/Effects/ScheduleEffects.cs`)
- **AutoMapper**:
  - **Why**: reduces boilerplate mapping between EF entities and UI/state DTOs; use for copy/clone operations too
  - **Where**: profiles in `src/Bible.Alarm/Stores/Mapping/**` (e.g. schedule mappings)
  - **Rule**: use AutoMapper for copy/clone (see `automapper-copy-clone.mdc`)
- **Polly**:
  - **Why**: resilient handling of flaky networks + transient file locks (SQLite/WAL, Android file handles)
  - **Where**: downloads (`DownloadService`), file ops (`MediaIndexService`), UI wait helpers
- **Quartz**:
  - **Why**: robust Cron parsing for “next fire time” calculation
  - **Important**: not used as a job scheduler; OS notifications + periodic jobs do the real scheduling
  - **Where**: `AlarmSchedule.NextFireDate()` in `src/Bible.Alarm.Shared/Models/Schedule/AlarmSchedule.cs`
- **CommunityToolkit**:
  - **Why**: lightweight MVVM primitives (messaging) + MediaElement-based playback integration
  - **Where**: `WeakReferenceMessenger` (system control messages) and `UseMauiCommunityToolkitMediaElement()`
- **TagLibSharp**:
  - **Why**: extract title/artwork from cached audio files for a richer “Now Playing” experience
  - **Where**: metadata display / platform now-playing services

